# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
# Syntax: a path pattern at column 0, then indented "Header: value" lines.
# A blank line ends a block, so keep comments outside the blocks.

# Cache policy: nothing here is ever reused from a browser's store.
#
# This site is a single unversioned file. There are no hashed asset names, so
# there is no way for a stale copy to be "partially" old — a cached index.html
# pins a visitor to an entire old version of the site, and there is nothing
# else on the page that benefits from being cached.
#
# no-store is what actually forbids reuse; no-cache/must-revalidate/max-age=0
# repeat the intent for implementations that handle one but not another, and
# Pragma/Expires cover ancient intermediary proxies.
#
# The cost is one round trip per visit (~11 KB gzipped). It is NOT a cold
# origin fetch: Cloudflare's edge still serves it, and the edge is purged on
# every deploy, so visitors always get the current build at edge speed.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, max-age=0
  Pragma: no-cache
  Expires: 0
